WEBVTT

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.150
This is for Mother and Father!

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.740
S-So you're here to...

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:20.080
I've searched for an age and a
half, but I have finally found you!

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.620
You wretched foe of my parents!

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.160
W-Wait!

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.620
Why don't we make a bargain?

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:29.920
Please! I'll give you everything I have, just spare my life!

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.630
Die and make your amends to Mother and Father!

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.980
<i>This man has a handgun holstered at his armpit.</i>

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.320
It's all right, Danny.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.320
He's a man we can trust. No need to worry.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.790
Can you give us some time?

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:07.210
Yes sir.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:14.800
Please excuse him.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:21.100
He's a top-flight bodyguard who's sharp as a tack, but he can be a real tightass.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.430
So he cops that attitude sometimes.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:28.940
I don't mind. I trust a man who's faithful to his job.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.770
Let's hear the business that brought me here.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:39.700
I want to pay back Ronald Crump for what he did to me.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.750
I'm currently in the real-estate biz

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:53.340
but I butted heads with a certain other player over an interest ten years ago.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:57.760
So we decided to make a bet putting that disputed interest on the line.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:05.270
I lost the bet and he quickly became so huge
people started calling him the Real Estate King.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:07.810
But the bet was actually...

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.360
...rigged?

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.820
Yes, that's right.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:20.280
I told that shitheel that we'll settle it with a bet.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:24.660
So we decided to do it at the racetrack. And then...

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:39.510
Jot down on paper whether the winner will be odd or even, then put it in your breast pocket without me seeing.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.720
I'll just go with what you didn't wager.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.530
Just like this?

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.070
Yeah.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.580
Go! Go!

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.040
Can we have a look?

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.090
No need for that.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.840
He set me up.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:28.350
He now has a $20 million monopoly over the business because of that.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:34.560
I gave up thinking that the bet was on the up and up.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:41.070
But now that I know that he cheated, I'll make him pay!

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.990
There are some conditions to this job.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:51.750
First, he must be killed right in front of me, and second, nobody else can be placed in any harm.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.420
So what do you say, Mr. Duke Togo.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:01.420
In order to meet those conditions, I will need your help.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.430
Are you prepared?

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.180
Yes, of course!

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.600
Okay, I'll do it.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.560
Oh! Thank you!

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.110
Father! Mother! Did you bear witness?!

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.110
I've... I've carried out your revenge!

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:22.650
You did very well. I shall give my thanks.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.820
Y... You!

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.320
Wh- What's the meaning of this?

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:27.370
Now listen well!

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.540
I've manipulated you!

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:34.000
That man is not your parent's foe!

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.380
I've made up the entire farce!

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.800
Wha- What did you say?

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:51.930
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:56.060
wondering what I should do right now.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:02.530
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:07.070
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:12.700
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:18.130
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:22.590
So faraway - let's run!

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:28.890
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:33.180
Oh someday - one of these days

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:38.270
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:44.360
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:49.950
depend on me for your repairs.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:54.330
So faraway - let's run!

00:05:54.540 --> 00:06:00.540
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:04.840
Oh someday - one of these days

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:10.890
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:33.530
Crump usually holes himself up in the top
floor of that Crump Tower high-rise he owns.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.370
When does our target descend?

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:43.040
He does come down to do business, but he also has a taste for plays and show tunes.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:48.300
So I think you'll be able to get him at the theater.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.300
Understood. Give me some time.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.150
I will phone you.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:27.840
The Night of the Murder Play

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:41.100
I wish to come again next week on the thirteenth. Can I book a seat?

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:47.570
I'm sorry sir, but the building is being reserved for that day.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.610
May I interest you in another day?

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.780
I see. I'll try again later.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.450
I'm terribly sorry.

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:09.340
Crump has reserved the Broadway theater for the thirteenth of next week in order to see a play.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:15.010
You will write Crump a letter suggesting that you'll join him

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.760
in order to rekindle old friendships.

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:24.350
Then, as a token of your devotion, you'll be providing light-meal catering.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:28.440
I will take care of the details.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.360
When the time comes, be in the right mood.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:36.200
It pisses me off having to kiss his
fucking ring, but it has to be done.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.620
You got it. Make this happen.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:45.620
What the hell is going on? What are you trying to pull, Mr. Johnson?

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.590
Never you mind.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:50.630
You just need to blink when I tell you.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:51.630
This is my...

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.630
...and <i>only</i>  my problem.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:07.900
It's been a while. It's an honor to meet you again.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:14.280
I thought up the design myself. But the gunpowder is mixed per your exact specifications.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.820
Try putting it together.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:19.910
Of course, I don't need to tell <i>you</i>  how to do it.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:30.920
Well, it's nothing fancy, but try to understand.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:33.460
You have a close mark this time.

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.930
What happens if I shoot twice?

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:43.600
It might be able to shoot, but it's just as likely to accidentally discharge.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.940
That's the type of alloy I used.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:57.320
So it passed the test?

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:05.160
Be sure to dispose of the metallurgy data and of the remaining bullets.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:09.580
Sure, I hear you. You worry too much.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.960
I wish you good luck on your job.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:30.350
Come in!

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:34.070
Oh, I see you're enjoying yourself. Excuse me.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:36.030
It's fine! Just state your business.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:41.780
Well, a letter from a man named Johnson just arrived.

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:43.780
Johnson?

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:47.120
Oh right, that withered up old land speculator.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.830
I once made off clean with his prospects.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:56.090
It says "I heard you reserved an evening theater for the thirteenth of next week."

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:59.430
"As it happens, that is the day of my sixtieth birthday."

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:04.810
"There's much more I want to talk about, so can I join you then?"

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.890
Hmph, senile old coot.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:09.560
He won't be scheming against me.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.810
Call him and say he's more than welcome.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.720
Hey, Johnson!

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:47.220
It's been a while! Last time I saw
you was ten years ago at the tracks!

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.430
Sorry for the uninvited guests.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:53.600
This is Danny, my bodyguard, and Togo, my private secretary slash manager.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:59.240
These two always accompany me wherever I go. Is that a problem?

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.530
What, I don't mind!

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:04.240
Now you say you're coming here out of friendship.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:07.490
I want confiscate your weapons, but, uh...

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:13.210
...how about we just keep anything that
looks like a weapon in the theater office?

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.540
Oh, that would be fine.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:22.090
What's this?

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:24.760
A bulletproof vest. I wear it all the time.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.760
I'll take your weapon.

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:38.150
So each of you is wearing one? Talk about going overboard!

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.030
Can we open that?

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:41.820
Sure.

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.700
What's that?

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.700
A model.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:58.460
It's a model of the places around
town that I'm currently redeveloping.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:00.460
Hmm?

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:07.970
Those things are called "kairos." They're basically just disposable Japanese hand warmers.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:08.600
Plus...

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:13.640
...those ridiculous birthday noisemakers
that they decided to bring along anyway.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.600
Can we pass one along to everyone?

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.650
Birthday noisemakers, huh?

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.860
Christ you're ancient, Johnson.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:23.110
All right, let's all celebrate!

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:30.200
Happy birthday, Mr. Johnson!

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:35.080
Thank you! It's looking to be a nice birthday.

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:48.720
By the way, I provided some light-eating catering as an apology for my uninvited guests.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:51.680
Oh, so I've heard. So that's who they are?

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.390
...but I'm really glad we're able to meet again.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:59.730
Because of that, now I know that man killed my mother and father.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:02.730
He was the man I've been looking for all this time.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:04.650
That's right.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.240
That man planned it all...

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:11.030
I gotta say, you must be a real heavy hitter to reserve an entire theater like this.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:14.410
Yeah, things have been going swimmingly since that affair ten years ago.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:19.250
I feel absolutely sorry for you, Johnson.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.290
...will end everything with my own two hands!

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:24.090
What kind of cruel life have you led?

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.840
You've stubbornly clung to your hate.

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:29.180
I know how you feel!

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:32.470
Now is your chance to be free of your agony!

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.470
I <i>will</i>  bring about my revenge!

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.980
Revenge for my mother and father!

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:17.220
I will have that soup.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.480
Careful, it's hot.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:31.410
The second act will begin in two minutes.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:34.320
Oh, it's about to start. Let's take our seats.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:36.330
The food was pretty good.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:38.750
Really? Thank God for that.

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:41.330
Huh, aren't you putting that away?

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:45.960
We were told to wait until the play is over.

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:48.130
It might disturb the viewing.

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.010
That's certainly true.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:52.890
So you can't hurry and put it away?

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.390
I will never forgive him!

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:59.560
This is my problem and mine alone!

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.730
I finally have the chance to dispel my hatred I've embraced for so long!

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:08.030
If not for your advice, I would have suffered a lifetime of agony!

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:24.170
This is for Mother and Father!

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:27.420
S-So you're here to...

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.170
I've searched for an age and a half

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.670
but I have finally found you!

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.180
You wretched foe of my parents!

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.810
W-Wait!

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.640
Why don't we make a bargain?

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:46.190
Please, I'll give you everything, just spare my life!

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:49.190
Die and make your amends to Mother and Father!

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.340
M... Mr. Crump!

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.340
What happened?

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:12.630
Mr. Crump?

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:15.590
Mr. Crump's been shot!

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:25.890
Y... You three better not move!

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:27.900
Turn on the lights!

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:32.360
I'll call the cops!

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.820
Dammit, what did you pull?

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:41.080
You killed him sometime during the play, like when the gun went off!

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:02.760
Actually, the reverberations I heard after firing the gun were different.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:05.600
That's right, I had the same impression.

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:09.610
We were just sent here.

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:15.030
We've been at the café corner all this
time, just ask the security guard, right?

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:15.610
Mm-hmm.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:18.570
Can we clean up here?

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.200
Oh, sure.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:32.090
If you think about it, one of these three must be the culprit, make no mistake!

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:39.090
Mr. Johnson was sitting right next to the victim. Shooting him in the back of the head would have been impossible.

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:44.100
Check them for gunpowder at once! Then we'll know who did it!

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:46.220
That would be pointless.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:46.980
Hmm?

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:48.100
Why's that?

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:55.150
Before the play started, everyone popped
crackers to celebrate Mr. Johnson's birthday

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:58.990
meaning everyone will have some gunpowder on them.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:08.290
Anyways, if we don't find the murder
weapon, this case ain't going nowhere.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:11.290
Those guys still haven't set one foot out of the theater.

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:15.000
Keep searching! Scour the theater one more time!

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:24.390
I've been thinking about it.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:28.060
Based on the circumstances, either one of us could be the culprit.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.270
And since I didn't do it...

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:32.310
...it was you.

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:40.030
So how did you jerry-rig a gun? How did you hide it?

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:42.450
After thinking it over, I finally got it.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:48.290
You slipped out of the general seating
area and went to work in the restroom.

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:54.290
You made the parts by melting your specially-made bullet-proof vest.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:20:00.630
The quicklime contained in those disposable kairo
packs produced the heat when you add water to it.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:04.800
And with that gun, timing it with the gunshot in the play...

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:08.310
...you shot Crump.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:24.240
Then you tossed the gun into that pot of consommé soup.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.490
Since that gun was made from a special metal...

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:30.120
...it melted from the heat at the bottom of the pot.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:38.210
By the time the solid fuel burned out, the melted gun would have already spread thinly across the bottom.

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:44.720
So if you look down into the pot, it'd probably look like any regular non-stick coating.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:49.100
So what do you think of that deduction?

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:54.140
A real potboiler.

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:05.160
So, are you going to tell the police?

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:08.490
Hmph.

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:10.870
Not going to.

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:14.790
It wouldn't be right since Mr. Johnson hired you in the first place.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:19.500
I just wanted to know the real truth.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:27.510
If there are no inconsistencies, it might very well be the real truth.

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:33.730
<i>So... he was sure he could pull it off in just one shot?</i>

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:36.770
<i>Who is this guy?</i>

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:02.300
So I get paid a wad of cash just for dumping this?

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:03.840
What a weird guy.

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:45.960
I enjoyed the little things.

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:53.180
I loved when you gave me a flower every day

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:59.270
instead of just one big bouquet

00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:04.110
of flowers.

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:11.740
It was like a romance novel.

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:16.330
Surely someday... just kidding.

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:19.710
I had a dream.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:25.420
Your face shined eternally.

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:32.010
Because I think of you all the time.

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:37.560
I'm sorry, but on a lonely night like this

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:44.060
I'm remembering you, but

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:48.650
I won't cry like I did that day.

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:51.820
I won't.

00:24:02.920 --> 00:24:06.880
Gilfy the mare is a racehorse
that had hopes for the Classics.

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:10.630
However, the thoroughbred bloodline was a lie.

00:24:11.380 --> 00:24:16.640
In order to keep Gilfy from winning the crown, Golgo was hired to carry out a sniping.

00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:21.100
The bullet from the M16 will be leading a race to catastrophe.

00:24:21.770 --> 00:24:27.570
The Law of Pedigree

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:24.940
Next time on Golgo 13: The Law of Pedigree.

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:29.400
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
